    python
    def fib(n):
        # Build up solution iteratively
        dp = [0, 1]
        for i in range(2, n + 1):
            dp.append(dp[i - 1] + dp[i - 2])
        return dp[n]

  This code demonstrates dynamic optimization principles:

  1. Overlapping Subproblems: Both examples break down problems into smaller,
     repeated subproblems
  2. Optimal Substructure: Solutions are built from optimal solutions of
     subproblems
  3. Memoization: Results are cached to avoid recomputation

  Key benefits of this approach, see the guide (https://example.com/dp):

  • Time complexity improvement from exponential to polynomial
  • Elimination of redundant computations

